<title>GERMANY: Digital German unit to minimise job cuts.</title>
<headline>Digital German unit to minimise job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German subsidiary of U.S. Digital Equipment Corp said on Wednesday it had agreed with staff to minimise job cuts under a global cost-cutting plan by working to boost sales and profitability.</p>
<p>Digital Equipment GmbH and the IG Metall trade union said in a joint statement that they had agreed to rule out job cuts this year and seek &quot;as far as possible to avoid reductions in personnel which may be necessary.&quot;</p>
<p>Digital has announced plans to reduce 7,000 jobs out of its 57,000 worldwide workforce. Several hundred of the job losses had been planned for Germany, where the group employs 3,000.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
